   "basis": "read",
   "text": "G0073 (agōn) is not a vice at all but a positive athletic and military metaphor for perseverance. Every one of its 6 verses is Paul or Hebrews describing his own or the believer's faithful effort: fight the good fight of the faith (1 Tim 6:12), I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race (2 Tim 4:7), run with endurance the race that is set before us (Heb 12:1). Nothing in this strong's verse set describes wrongdoing, discord or a moral failure of any kind; its inclusion in the cluster looks like a gloss-text accident (the English word fight) and not a thematic match, a candidate for a cluster_strong review.",
