   "text": "H4421 (milchamah, 91 verses, the single largest strong across all 14 families) is almost entirely literal armed warfare between nations and armies: man of war, troop counts, battle-line narrative (1 Chr, 2 Chr, Judges, Samuel). A handful of verses apply it to God metaphorically (the LORD is a man of war, Exod 15:3; mighty in battle, Ps 24:8), but the overwhelming majority is straightforward military-historical narration, not moral vocabulary about an inner disposition at all.",
